            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joe and Jill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! If you're looking for a classic lime daiquiri for yourself or for guests, this will be a big hit for all. We didn't change a thing for our monthly neighborhood Mexican night, and everyone raved!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "azurite"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was tasty enough. The appeal of this recipe is that it is really easy. It is good for a quick throw-together. The problems the adults in our family had with this was first, it was too sweet. We ended up adding a lot more ice. I think the sparkling water one other reviewer used would probably have helped a lot with the sweetness. Two, it was very strong. I cut the rum down to 8 oz instead of twelve, and even then it was potent. I think this recipe is a good place to start, but definitely needs some tweaking.\n\nUpdate: I made this again. I only use HALF the concentrate. I used seltzer water to make up the difference, plus a bit extra until it was more of a slushy consistency rather than thick. Again, only 8 oz of the alcohol, not twelve. I also added in a couple of limes wedges, without peel, into the blender and blended that all in. Now it is the perfect daiquiri. I hate rating a recipe when I have changed it up so much. But this was a good start. Just wrong proportions.",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-25T19:40:20.340Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
